WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:15.380
In this course, API means C++ interfaces broadly: library functions, internal component boundaries, plugin contracts, callback interfaces, service integration layers, and classes that control access to sensitive state.

2
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:22.380
An API is a security boundary because it shapes what callers can express and what mistakes are easy to make.

3
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:26.720
A narrow, explicit interface can guide callers toward safe behavior.

4
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:31.620
A vague interface can spread hidden assumptions across many call sites.

5
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.700
Secure API design does not rely on every caller remembering private rules.

6
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:42.480
It makes valid use obvious, invalid use difficult, and security-sensitive behavior explicit.

7
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:48.980
The interface itself should help reviewers understand what is trusted, who owns data, and what happens on failure.

8
00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.900
This matters even for internal code.

9
00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:01.920
A parser boundary, plugin hook, scripting bridge, or low-level library can receive data or requests that should be validated before they influence sensitive state.

10
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:14.680
API design connects many topics: ownership, lifetime, input validation, access control, error handling, logging, resource cleanup, and long-term compatibility.

11
00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.460
A small interface decision can affect hundreds of future calls.

12
00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:22.500
The goal is not to make every function heavy or bureaucratic.

13
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:32.680
The goal is to put security expectations in the type system, naming, contracts, and failure behavior so future maintainers can use the API safely.

14
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:38.880
A good secure API reduces review burden because its shape carries part of the security design.

15
00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:47.160
That shape is especially important in shared libraries and platform components, where one unclear decision can be copied for years.

16
00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.520
Design the boundary so the safe call is the natural call.
